virglrenderer: remember the index range of an index buffer until it is written

What: an indexed draw reads its indices back from the GL buffer and scans them for
the smallest and largest index (virgl-draw-range-checks.patch). Each index buffer
now keeps its last four ranges (offset, count, index size, restart, restart index ->
min, max) with the buffer's write count (content_gen) at the read. Every write vrend
makes to a buffer from the CPU goes through vrend_resource_contents_changed()
(transfers, inline writes and copy transfers in vrend_renderer_transfer_write_iov,
video encode output), which makes the old ranges stale. A buffer the GPU writes or
the guest may map is marked with vrend_resource_no_index_range_cache() where it is
written, bound or mapped (buffer copies, stream output targets, storage buffers,
images, atomic counters, query results, blob resources, resource_map) and is read
back on every draw from then on; the mark is never cleared. A GPU write runs in its
own GL context's order, so another GL context (a guest's second context or sub
context) could read the indices back before it lands; it is never cached. Only plain GL buffers are cached: no persistent, coherent,
immutable, memory-object, GBM, host-memory, blob or imported storage. A read is kept
only when no GL error is pending after it (a refused read skips the draw, as the
check before the GL draw call would, and is read again next time).
OMACVM_VIRGL_INDEX_RANGE_CACHE=0 reads back on every draw again (the code path from
before); qemu.log says which at start. OMACVM_VIRGL_CACHE_STATS=1 logs hits, misses
and uncached draws every 10 s.
Why: pages that draw each object on its own read the same indices tens of thousands
of times a frame. WebGL Aquarium at 30,000 fish makes ~31,000 indexed draws a frame;
the read-back (two binds, glGetBufferSubData, the scan) was 9 % of QEMU's render
thread on a Mac mini M4.
Upstream: depends on virgl-draw-range-checks.patch (OmacVM only); not sent.
Tests: Tests/virgl/test-index-range-cache.c (soft GL + gl-oracle; every write path,
each GPU-write binding, each part of the key, a refused read; run with the switch on
and off), Tests/virgl/index-range-writes.py (every GL call in src/ that can write a
buffer is on a reviewed list and bumps or marks), Tests/virgl/mutate-index-range-cache.py
(manual: each bump, mark, check and key compare taken out alone fails the test).

